REPLACE INTO `concept_description` (`concept_description_id`, `concept_id`, `description`, `locale`, `creator`, `date_created`, `changed_by`, `date_changed`, `uuid`) values('5649','119310','Disorders of the anterior or posterior pituitary gland which usually manifest as hypersecretion or hyposecretion of pituitary hormones. Pituitary mass lesions may also produce compression of the OPTIC CHIASM and other adjacent structures.','en','1','2007-10-18 04:28:24','1',NULL,'5649FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF');
REPLACE INTO `concept_description` (`concept_description_id`, `concept_id`, `description`, `locale`, `creator`, `date_created`, `changed_by`, `date_changed`, `uuid`) values('5650','119311','Diminution or cessation of secretion of one or more hormones from the anterior pituitary gland (including LH; FSH; SOMATOTROPIN; and CORTICOTROPIN). This may result from surgical or radiation ablation, non-secretory PITUITARY NEOPLASMS, metastatic tumors, infarction, PITUITARY APOPLEXY, infiltrative or granulomatous processes, and other conditions.','en','1','2007-10-18 04:28:24','1',NULL,'5650FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF');
REPLACE INTO `concept_description` (`concept_description_id`, `concept_id`, `description`, `locale`, `creator`, `date_created`, `changed_by`, `date_changed`, `uuid`) values('5651','119316','Metabolic disorders affecting amino acid metabolism. They are present at birth, although they may not become symptomatic until later in life. The majority of these disorders are inherited and present in the neonatal period with metabolic disturbances (e.g., ACIDOSIS) and neurologic manifestations.','en','1','2007-10-18 04:28:24','1',NULL,'5651FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF');
REPLACE INTO `concept_description` (`concept_description_id`, `concept_id`, `description`, `locale`, `creator`, `date_created`, `changed_by`, `date_changed`, `uuid`) values('5652','119323','A form of ocular misalignment where the visual axes diverge inappropriately. For example, medial rectus muscle weakness may produce this condition as the affected eye will deviate laterally upon attempted forward gaze. An exotropia occurs due to the relatively unopposed force exerted on the eye by the lateral rectus muscle, which pulls the eye in an outward direction.','en','1','2007-10-18 04:28:24','1',NULL,'5652FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF');
REPLACE INTO `concept_description` (`concept_description_id`, `concept_id`, `description`, `locale`, `creator`, `date_created`, `changed_by`, `date_changed`, `uuid`) values('5653','119326','A skin and mucous membrane disease characterized by an eruption of macules, papules, nodules, vesicles, and/or bullae with characteristic \"bull\'s-eye\" lesions usually occurring on the dorsal aspect of the hands and forearms.','en','1','2007-10-18 04:28:24','1',NULL,'5653FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF');
REPLACE INTO `concept_description` (`concept_description_id`, `concept_id`, `description`, `locale`, `creator`, `date_created`, `changed_by`, `date_changed`, `uuid`) values('5656','119333','Displacement of one or more bones from their normal position within a joint.','en','1','2007-10-18 04:28:24','1',NULL,'5656FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF');
REPLACE INTO `concept_description` (`concept_description_id`, `concept_id`, `description`, `locale`, `creator`, `date_created`, `changed_by`, `date_changed`, `uuid`) values('5658','119348','Diseases of the peripheral nerves external to the brain and spinal cord, which includes diseases of the nerve roots, ganglia, plexi, autonomic nerves, sensory nerves, and motor nerves.','en','1','2007-10-18 04:28:24','1',NULL,'5658FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF');
REPLACE INTO `concept_description` (`concept_description_id`, `concept_id`, `description`, `locale`, `creator`, `date_created`, `changed_by`, `date_changed`, `uuid`) values('5660','119353','A mosquito-borne viral illness caused by the WEST NILE VIRUS, a FLAVIVIRUS and endemic to regions of Africa, Asia, and Europe. Common clinical features include HEADACHE, FEVER, maculopapular rash, gastrointestinal symptoms, and lymphadenopathy. MENINGITIS; ENCEPHALITIS; and MYELITIS may also occur. The disease may occasionally be fatal or leave survivors with residual neurologic deficits. (From Joynt, Clinical Neurology, 1996, Ch26, p13; Lancet 1998 Sep 5;352(9130):767-71)','en','1','2007-10-18 04:28:24','1',NULL,'5660FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF');
REPLACE INTO `concept_description` (`concept_description_id`, `concept_id`, `description`, `locale`, `creator`, `date_created`, `changed_by`, `date_changed`, `uuid`) values('5661','119354','Infections with nematodes of the superfamily FILARIOIDEA. The presence of living worms in the body is mainly asymptomatic but the death of adult worms leads to granulomatous inflammation and permanent fibrosis. Organisms of the genus Elaeophora infect wild elk and domestic sheep causing ischaemic necrosis of the brain, blindness, and dermatosis of the face.','en','1','2007-10-18 04:28:24','1','2016-05-27 02:47:59','5661FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF');
REPLACE INTO `concept_description` (`concept_description_id`, `concept_id`, `description`, `locale`, `creator`, `date_created`, `changed_by`, `date_changed`, `uuid`) values('5662','119356','Infection of humans or animals with hookworms other than those caused by the genus Ancylostoma or Necator, for which the specific terms ANCYLOSTOMIASIS and NECATORIASIS are available.','en','1','2007-10-18 04:28:24','1',NULL,'5662FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF');
REPLACE INTO `concept_description` (`concept_description_id`, `concept_id`, `description`, `locale`, `creator`, `date_created`, `changed_by`, `date_changed`, `uuid`) values('5663','119360','Infection with any of the rotaviruses. Specific infections include human infantile diarrhea, neonatal calf diarrhea, and epidemic diarrhea of infant mice.','en','1','2007-10-18 04:28:24','1',NULL,'5663FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF');
REPLACE INTO `concept_description` (`concept_description_id`, `concept_id`, `description`, `locale`, `creator`, `date_created`, `changed_by`, `date_changed`, `uuid`) values('5664','119361','A genus of PICORNAVIRIDAE inhabiting primarily the respiratory tract of mammalian hosts. It includes the human strains associated with common colds.','en','1','2007-10-18 04:28:24','1',NULL,'5664FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF');
REPLACE INTO `concept_description` (`concept_description_id`, `concept_id`, `description`, `locale`, `creator`, `date_created`, `changed_by`, `date_changed`, `uuid`) values('5665','119366','Family of RNA viruses that infects birds and mammals and encodes the enzyme reverse transcriptase. The family contains seven genera: HTLV-BLV VIRUSES; LENTIVIRUS; RETROVIRUSES TYPE B, MAMMALIAN; RETROVIRUSES TYPE C, AVIAN; RETROVIRUSES TYPE C, MAMMALIAN; RETROVIRUSES TYPE D; and SPUMAVIRUS. A key feature of retrovirus biology is the synthesis of a DNA copy of the genome which is integrated into cellular DNA. After integration it is sometimes not expressed but maintained in a latent state (PROVIRUSES).','en','1','2007-10-18 04:28:24','1',NULL,'5665FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF');
REPLACE INTO `concept_description` (`concept_description_id`, `concept_id`, `description`, `locale`, `creator`, `date_created`, `changed_by`, `date_changed`, `uuid`) values('5666','119369','Family of RNA viruses that infects birds and mammals and encodes the enzyme reverse transcriptase. The family contains seven genera: HTLV-BLV VIRUSES; LENTIVIRUS; RETROVIRUSES TYPE B, MAMMALIAN; RETROVIRUSES TYPE C, AVIAN; RETROVIRUSES TYPE C, MAMMALIAN; RETROVIRUSES TYPE D; and SPUMAVIRUS. A key feature of retrovirus biology is the synthesis of a DNA copy of the genome which is integrated into cellular DNA. After integration it is sometimes not expressed but maintained in a latent state (PROVIRUSES).','en','1','2007-10-18 04:28:24','1',NULL,'5666FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF');
REPLACE INTO `concept_description` (`concept_description_id`, `concept_id`, `description`, `locale`, `creator`, `date_created`, `changed_by`, `date_changed`, `uuid`) values('5667','119373','Infections with viruses of the genus PARAMYXOVIRUS, family PARAMYXOVIRIDAE. Host cell infection occurs by adsorption, via hemagglutinin, to the cell surface.','en','1','2007-10-18 04:28:24','1',NULL,'5667FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF');
REPLACE INTO `concept_description` (`concept_description_id`, `concept_id`, `description`, `locale`, `creator`, `date_created`, `changed_by`, `date_changed`, `uuid`) values('5668','119374','Infections with viruses of the family PARAMYXOVIRIDAE. This includes MORBILLIVIRUS INFECTIONS, PARAMYXOVIRUS INFECTIONS, PNEUMOVIRUS INFECTIONS, and RUBULAVIRUS INFECTIONS.','en','1','2007-10-18 04:28:24','1',NULL,'5668FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF');
REPLACE INTO `concept_description` (`concept_description_id`, `concept_id`, `description`, `locale`, `creator`, `date_created`, `changed_by`, `date_changed`, `uuid`) values('5669','119375','Infections by nematodes, general or unspecified.','en','1','2007-10-18 04:28:24','1',NULL,'5669FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF');
REPLACE INTO `concept_description` (`concept_description_id`, `concept_id`, `description`, `locale`, `creator`, `date_created`, `changed_by`, `date_changed`, `uuid`) values('5671','119379','Infestations by parasites which live on the outside of the body of the host.','en','1','2007-10-18 04:28:24','1',NULL,'5671FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF');
REPLACE INTO `concept_description` (`concept_description_id`, `concept_id`, `description`, `locale`, `creator`, `date_created`, `changed_by`, `date_changed`, `uuid`) values('5672','119381','Virus diseases caused by the ADENOVIRIDAE.','en','1','2007-10-18 04:28:24','1',NULL,'5672FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF');
REPLACE INTO `concept_description` (`concept_description_id`, `concept_id`, `description`, `locale`, `creator`, `date_created`, `changed_by`, `date_changed`, `uuid`) values('5674','119383','Infections by the genus RICKETTSIA.','en','1','2007-10-18 04:28:24','1',NULL,'5674FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF');
REPLACE INTO `concept_description` (`concept_description_id`, `concept_id`, `description`, `locale`, `creator`, `date_created`, `changed_by`, `date_changed`, `uuid`) values('5676','119387','Infections or infestations with parasitic organisms. They are often contracted through contact with an intermediate vector, but may occur as the result of direct exposure.','en','1','2007-10-18 04:28:24','1','2016-05-27 20:40:23','5676FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF');
REPLACE INTO `concept_description` (`concept_description_id`, `concept_id`, `description`, `locale`, `creator`, `date_created`, `changed_by`, `date_changed`, `uuid`) values('5678','119392','A symptom complex of unknown etiology, that is characteristic of a particular abnormality.','en','1','2007-10-18 04:28:24','1',NULL,'5678FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF');
REPLACE INTO `concept_description` (`concept_description_id`, `concept_id`, `description`, `locale`, `creator`, `date_created`, `changed_by`, `date_changed`, `uuid`) values('5679','119394','A congenital cardiovascular malformation in which the aorta arises entirely from the right ventricle and the pulmonary artery from the left ventricle, so that the venous return from the peripheral circulation is recirculated by the right ventricle via the aorta to the systemic circulation without being oxygenated in the lungs.','en','1','2007-10-18 04:28:24','1',NULL,'5679FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF');
REPLACE INTO `concept_description` (`concept_description_id`, `concept_id`, `description`, `locale`, `creator`, `date_created`, `changed_by`, `date_changed`, `uuid`) values('5680','119395','A heterogeneous group of nonprogressive motor disorders caused by chronic brain injuries that originate in the prenatal period, perinatal period, or first few years of life. The four major subtypes are spastic, athetoid, ataxic, and mixed cerebral palsy, with spastic forms being the most common. The motor disorder may range from difficulties with fine motor control to severe spasticity (see MUSCLE SPASTICITY) in all limbs. Spastic diplegia (Little disease) is the most common subtype, and is characterized by spasticity that is more prominent in the legs than in the arms. Pathologically, this condition may be associated with LEUKOMALACIA, PERIVENTRICULAR. (From Dev Med Child Neurol 1998 Aug;40(8):520-7)','en','1','2007-10-18 04:28:24','1',NULL,'5680FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF');
REPLACE INTO `concept_description` (`concept_description_id`, `concept_id`, `description`, `locale`, `creator`, `date_created`, `changed_by`, `date_changed`, `uuid`) values('5681','119396','A heterogeneous group of nonprogressive motor disorders caused by chronic brain injuries that originate in the prenatal period, perinatal period, or first few years of life. The four major subtypes are spastic, athetoid, ataxic, and mixed cerebral palsy, with spastic forms being the most common. The motor disorder may range from difficulties with fine motor control to severe spasticity (see MUSCLE SPASTICITY) in all limbs. Spastic diplegia (Little disease) is the most common subtype, and is characterized by spasticity that is more prominent in the legs than in the arms. Pathologically, this condition may be associated with LEUKOMALACIA, PERIVENTRICULAR. (From Dev Med Child Neurol 1998 Aug;40(8):520-7)','en','1','2007-10-18 04:28:24','1',NULL,'5681FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF');
REPLACE INTO `concept_description` (`concept_description_id`, `concept_id`, `description`, `locale`, `creator`, `date_created`, `changed_by`, `date_changed`, `uuid`) values('5682','119399','A localized infection of mucous membranes or skin caused by toxigenic strains of CORYNEBACTERIUM DIPHTHERIAE. It is characterized by the presence of a pseudomembrane at the site of infection. DIPHTHERIA TOXIN, produced by C. diphtheriae, can cause myocarditis, polyneuritis, and other systemic toxic effects.','en','1','2007-10-18 04:28:24','1','2016-05-27 02:47:32','5682FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF');
REPLACE INTO `concept_description` (`concept_description_id`, `concept_id`, `description`, `locale`, `creator`, `date_created`, `changed_by`, `date_changed`, `uuid`) values('5683','119403','A syndrome characterized by cardiac enlargement and congestive heart failure. It probably represents the end result of many forms of myocardial damage produced by a variety of toxic, metabolic, or infectious agents.','en','1','2007-10-18 04:28:24','1',NULL,'5683FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF');
REPLACE INTO `concept_description` (`concept_description_id`, `concept_id`, `description`, `locale`, `creator`, `date_created`, `changed_by`, `date_changed`, `uuid`) values('5685','119407','Disorders affecting the motor function of the upper or lower esophageal sphincters, the esophageal body, or a combination of these parts. The failure of the sphincters to maintain a tonic pressure may result in the impeding of the passage of food, regurgitation of food, or reflux of gastric acid into the esophagus.','en','1','2007-10-18 04:28:24','1',NULL,'5685FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF');
REPLACE INTO `concept_description` (`concept_description_id`, `concept_id`, `description`, `locale`, `creator`, `date_created`, `changed_by`, `date_changed`, `uuid`) values('5686','119409','The most common aggressive form of non-Hodgkin lymphoma. It occurs in both diffuse and nodular form. The large cells may have cleaved and non-cleaved nuclei.','en','1','2007-10-18 04:28:24','1',NULL,'5686FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF');
REPLACE INTO `concept_description` (`concept_description_id`, `concept_id`, `description`, `locale`, `creator`, `date_created`, `changed_by`, `date_changed`, `uuid`) values('5687','119410','Malignant lymphoma in which neoplastic cells diffusely infiltrate the entire lymph node without any definite organized pattern. Patients whose lymphomas present a diffuse pattern generally have a more unfavorable survival outlook than those presenting with a follicular or nodular pattern.','en','1','2007-10-18 04:28:24','1',NULL,'5687FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF');
REPLACE INTO `concept_description` (`concept_description_id`, `concept_id`, `description`, `locale`, `creator`, `date_created`, `changed_by`, `date_changed`, `uuid`) values('5688','119411','Malignant lymphoma characterized by the presence of immunoblasts with uniformly round-to-oval nuclei, one or more prominent nucleoli, and abundant cytoplasm. This class may be subdivided into plasmacytoid and clear-cell types based on cytoplasmic characteristics. A third category, pleomorphous, may be analogous to some of the peripheral T-cell lymphomas (LYMPHOMA, T-CELL, PERIPHERAL) recorded in both the United States and Japan.','en','1','2007-10-18 04:28:24','1',NULL,'5688FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF');
REPLACE INTO `concept_description` (`concept_description_id`, `concept_id`, `description`, `locale`, `creator`, `date_created`, `changed_by`, `date_changed`, `uuid`) values('5690','119413','An acquired organic mental disorder with loss of intellectual abilities of sufficient severity to interfere with social or occupational functioning. The dysfunction is multifaceted and involves memory, behavior, personality, judgment, attention, spatial relations, language, abstract thought, and other executive functions. The intellectual decline is usually progressive, and initially spares the level of consciousness.','en','1','2007-10-18 04:28:24','1',NULL,'5690FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF');
REPLACE INTO `concept_description` (`concept_description_id`, `concept_id`, `description`, `locale`, `creator`, `date_created`, `changed_by`, `date_changed`, `uuid`) values('5691','119414','Chronic inflammation and progressive fibrosis of the pulmonary alveolar walls, with steadily progressive dyspnea, resulting finally in death from oxygen lack or right heart failure.','en','1','2007-10-18 04:28:24','1',NULL,'5691FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF');
REPLACE INTO `concept_description` (`concept_description_id`, `concept_id`, `description`, `locale`, `creator`, `date_created`, `changed_by`, `date_changed`, `uuid`) values('5692','119415','Chronic inflammation and progressive fibrosis of the pulmonary alveolar walls, with steadily progressive dyspnea, resulting finally in death from oxygen lack or right heart failure.','en','1','2007-10-18 04:28:24','1',NULL,'5692FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF');
REPLACE INTO `concept_description` (`concept_description_id`, `concept_id`, `description`, `locale`, `creator`, `date_created`, `changed_by`, `date_changed`, `uuid`) values('5693','119416','Diffuse enlargement of the thyroid gland.','en','1','2007-10-18 04:28:24','1',NULL,'5693FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF');
REPLACE INTO `concept_description` (`concept_description_id`, `concept_id`, `description`, `locale`, `creator`, `date_created`, `changed_by`, `date_changed`, `uuid`) values('5694','119417','Enlargement of the thyroid gland.','en','1','2007-10-18 04:28:24','1',NULL,'5694FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF');
REPLACE INTO `concept_description` (`concept_description_id`, `concept_id`, `description`, `locale`, `creator`, `date_created`, `changed_by`, `date_changed`, `uuid`) values('5695','119418','Acute and chronic (see also BRAIN INJURIES, CHRONIC) injuries to the brain, including the cerebral hemispheres, CEREBELLUM, and BRAIN STEM. Clinical manifestations depend on the nature of injury. Diffuse trauma to the brain is frequently associated with DIFFUSE AXONAL INJURY or COMA, POST-TRAUMATIC. Localized injuries may be associated with NEUROBEHAVIORAL MANIFESTATIONS; HEMIPARESIS, or other focal neurologic deficits.','en','1','2007-10-18 04:28:24','1','2014-06-03 18:28:24','5695FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF');
REPLACE INTO `concept_description` (`concept_description_id`, `concept_id`, `description`, `locale`, `creator`, `date_created`, `changed_by`, `date_changed`, `uuid`) values('5696','119419','Communication through a system of conventional vocal symbols.','en','1','2007-10-18 04:28:24','1',NULL,'5696FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF');
REPLACE INTO `concept_description` (`concept_description_id`, `concept_id`, `description`, `locale`, `creator`, `date_created`, `changed_by`, `date_changed`, `uuid`) values('5697','119420','Disorders of voice pitch, loudness, or quality. Dysphonia refers to impaired utterance of sounds by the vocal folds.','en','1','2007-10-18 04:28:24','1',NULL,'5697FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF');
REPLACE INTO `concept_description` (`concept_description_id`, `concept_id`, `description`, `locale`, `creator`, `date_created`, `changed_by`, `date_changed`, `uuid`) values('5698','119421','Disorders of voice pitch, loudness, or quality. Dysphonia refers to impaired utterance of sounds by the vocal folds.','en','1','2007-10-18 04:28:24','1',NULL,'5698FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF');
REPLACE INTO `concept_description` (`concept_description_id`, `concept_id`, `description`, `locale`, `creator`, `date_created`, `changed_by`, `date_changed`, `uuid`) values('5699','119424','Heart decompensation in which the heart is unable to maintain adequate circulation of blood in the tissues of the body or to pump out the venous blood returned to it by the venous circulation.','en','1','2007-10-18 04:28:24','1',NULL,'5699FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF');
REPLACE INTO `concept_description` (`concept_description_id`, `concept_id`, `description`, `locale`, `creator`, `date_created`, `changed_by`, `date_changed`, `uuid`) values('5700','119428','An abnormal opening or fissure between two adjacent teeth.','en','1','2007-10-18 04:28:24','1',NULL,'5700FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF');
REPLACE INTO `concept_description` (`concept_description_id`, `concept_id`, `description`, `locale`, `creator`, `date_created`, `changed_by`, `date_changed`, `uuid`) values('5701','119429','Passage of excessively liquid or excessively frequent stools.','en','1','2007-10-18 04:28:24','1',NULL,'5701FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF');
REPLACE INTO `concept_description` (`concept_description_id`, `concept_id`, `description`, `locale`, `creator`, `date_created`, `changed_by`, `date_changed`, `uuid`) values('5703','119435','Peripheral, autonomic, and cranial nerve disorders that are associated with DIABETES MELLITUS. These conditions usually result from diabetic microvascular injury involving small blood vessels that supply nerves (VASA NERVORUM). Relatively common conditions which may be associated with diabetic neuropathy include third nerve palsy (see OCULOMOTOR NERVE DISEASES); MONONEUROPATHY; mononeuropathy multiplex; diabetic amyotrophy; a painful POLYNEUROPATHY; autonomic neuropathy; and thoracoabdominal neuropathy. (From Adams et al., Principles of Neurology, 6th ed, p1325)','en','1','2007-10-18 04:28:24','1',NULL,'5703FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF');
REPLACE INTO `concept_description` (`concept_description_id`, `concept_id`, `description`, `locale`, `creator`, `date_created`, `changed_by`, `date_changed`, `uuid`) values('5704','119438','Peripheral, autonomic, and cranial nerve disorders that are associated with DIABETES MELLITUS. These conditions usually result from diabetic microvascular injury involving small blood vessels that supply nerves (VASA NERVORUM). Relatively common conditions which may be associated with diabetic neuropathy include third nerve palsy (see OCULOMOTOR NERVE DISEASES); MONONEUROPATHY; mononeuropathy multiplex; diabetic amyotrophy; a painful POLYNEUROPATHY; autonomic neuropathy; and thoracoabdominal neuropathy. (From Adams et al., Principles of Neurology, 6th ed, p1325)','en','1','2007-10-18 04:28:24','1',NULL,'5704FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF');
REPLACE INTO `concept_description` (`concept_description_id`, `concept_id`, `description`, `locale`, `creator`, `date_created`, `changed_by`, `date_changed`, `uuid`) values('5706','119441','Complication of diabetes resulting from severe insulin deficiency coupled with an absolute or relative increase in glucagon concentration. The metabolic acidosis is caused by the breakdown of adipose stores and resulting increased levels of free fatty acids. Glucagon accelerates the oxidation of the free fatty acids producing excess ketone bodies (ketosis).','en','1','2007-10-18 04:28:24','1',NULL,'5706FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF');
REPLACE INTO `concept_description` (`concept_description_id`, `concept_id`, `description`, `locale`, `creator`, `date_created`, `changed_by`, `date_changed`, `uuid`) values('5715','119452','A heterogeneous group of disorders that share glucose intolerance in common.','en','1','2007-10-18 04:28:24','1',NULL,'5715FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF');
REPLACE INTO `concept_description` (`concept_description_id`, `concept_id`, `description`, `locale`, `creator`, `date_created`, `changed_by`, `date_changed`, `uuid`) values('5716','119453','A syndrome consisting of extreme hyperglycemia, serum hyperosmolarity and dehydration in the absence of ketosis and acidosis.','en','1','2007-10-18 04:28:24','1',NULL,'5716FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF');
