REPLACE INTO `concept_description` (`concept_description_id`, `concept_id`, `description`, `locale`, `creator`, `date_created`, `changed_by`, `date_changed`, `uuid`) values('12278','139407','Inflammation of the tongue.','en','1','2007-10-18 04:28:24','1',NULL,'12278FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF');
REPLACE INTO `concept_description` (`concept_description_id`, `concept_id`, `description`, `locale`, `creator`, `date_created`, `changed_by`, `date_changed`, `uuid`) values('12279','139409','An extremely common benign tumor, occurring most commonly in infancy and childhood, made up of newly formed blood vessels, and resulting from malformation of angioblastic tissue of fetal life. It can occur anywhere in the body but is most frequently noticed in the skin and subcutaneous tissues. About 75% are present at birth, and about 60% occur in the head and neck area. The majority in infancy will regress spontaneously. Some hemangiomas grow rapidly during the early months of life and may be a source of some concern, although virtually all disappear by about 5 years of age. They do not metastasize and simple excision will often be curative. (Dorland, 27th ed; from Stedman, 25th ed; DeVita Jr et al., Cancer: Principles & Practice of Oncology, 3d ed, p1355)','en','1','2007-10-18 04:28:24','1',NULL,'12279FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF');
REPLACE INTO `concept_description` (`concept_description_id`, `concept_id`, `description`, `locale`, `creator`, `date_created`, `changed_by`, `date_changed`, `uuid`) values('12280','139412','A disorder whose predominant feature is a loss or alteration in physical functioning that suggests a physical disorder but that is actually a direct expression of a psychological conflict or need.','en','1','2007-10-18 04:28:24','1',NULL,'12280FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF');
REPLACE INTO `concept_description` (`concept_description_id`, `concept_id`, `description`, `locale`, `creator`, `date_created`, `changed_by`, `date_changed`, `uuid`) values('12281','139413','A disorder whose predominant feature is a loss or alteration in physical functioning that suggests a physical disorder but that is actually a direct expression of a psychological conflict or need.','en','1','2007-10-18 04:28:24','1',NULL,'12281FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF');
REPLACE INTO `concept_description` (`concept_description_id`, `concept_id`, `description`, `locale`, `creator`, `date_created`, `changed_by`, `date_changed`, `uuid`) values('12282','139415','An autosomal recessive inherited sphingolipidosis caused by a deficiency of GALACTOSYLCERAMIDASE leading to an accumulation of PSYCHOSINE in LYSOSOMES of the BRAIN; PERIPHERAL NERVES; LIVER; KIDNEY; and LEUKOCYTES. In the nervous sytem there is prominent central and peripheral demyelination. The infantile form presents at age 4-6 months with psychomotor retardation, MUSCLE SPASTICITY, and tonic spasms induced by minor stimuli. Death occurs within two years. Later onset forms of this disease are characterized by a less fulminant course. (From Menkes, Textbook of Child Neurology, 5th ed, pp195-7)','en','1','2007-10-18 04:28:24','1',NULL,'12282FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF');
REPLACE INTO `concept_description` (`concept_description_id`, `concept_id`, `description`, `locale`, `creator`, `date_created`, `changed_by`, `date_changed`, `uuid`) values('12283','139416','An autosomal recessive inherited sphingolipidosis caused by a deficiency of GALACTOSYLCERAMIDASE leading to an accumulation of PSYCHOSINE in LYSOSOMES of the BRAIN; PERIPHERAL NERVES; LIVER; KIDNEY; and LEUKOCYTES. In the nervous sytem there is prominent central and peripheral demyelination. The infantile form presents at age 4-6 months with psychomotor retardation, MUSCLE SPASTICITY, and tonic spasms induced by minor stimuli. Death occurs within two years. Later onset forms of this disease are characterized by a less fulminant course. (From Menkes, Textbook of Child Neurology, 5th ed, pp195-7)','en','1','2007-10-18 04:28:24','1',NULL,'12283FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF');
REPLACE INTO `concept_description` (`concept_description_id`, `concept_id`, `description`, `locale`, `creator`, `date_created`, `changed_by`, `date_changed`, `uuid`) values('12284','139417','Congenital open-angle glaucoma that results from dysgenesis of the angle structures accompanied by increased intraocular pressure and enlargement of the eye. Treatment is both medical and surgical.','en','1','2007-10-18 04:28:24','1',NULL,'12284FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF');
REPLACE INTO `concept_description` (`concept_description_id`, `concept_id`, `description`, `locale`, `creator`, `date_created`, `changed_by`, `date_changed`, `uuid`) values('12285','139423','A condition in which the intraocular pressure is elevated above normal and which may lead to glaucoma.','en','1','2007-10-18 04:28:24','1',NULL,'12285FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF');
REPLACE INTO `concept_description` (`concept_description_id`, `concept_id`, `description`, `locale`, `creator`, `date_created`, `changed_by`, `date_changed`, `uuid`) values('12286','139431','An ocular disease, occurring in many forms, having as its primary characteristics an unstable or a sustained increase in the intraocular pressure which the eye cannot withstand without damage to its structure or impairment of its function. The consequences of the increased pressure may be manifested in a variety of symptoms, depending upon type and severity, such as excavation of the optic disk, hardness of the eyeball, corneal anesthesia, reduced visual acuity, seeing of colored halos around lights, disturbed dark adaptation, visual field defects, and headaches. (Dictionary of Visual Science, 4th ed)','en','1','2007-10-18 04:28:24','1',NULL,'12286FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF');
REPLACE INTO `concept_description` (`concept_description_id`, `concept_id`, `description`, `locale`, `creator`, `date_created`, `changed_by`, `date_changed`, `uuid`) values('12287','139433','A congenital bleeding disorder with prolonged bleeding time, absence of aggregation of platelets in response to most agents, especially ADP, and impaired or absent clot retraction. Platelet membranes are deficient in or have a defect in the glycoprotein IIb-IIIa complex (PLATELET GLYCOPROTEIN GPIIB-IIIA COMPLEX).','en','1','2007-10-18 04:28:24','1',NULL,'12287FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF');
REPLACE INTO `concept_description` (`concept_description_id`, `concept_id`, `description`, `locale`, `creator`, `date_created`, `changed_by`, `date_changed`, `uuid`) values('12289','139436','A contagious disease of horses that can be transmitted to humans. It is caused by Pseudomonas mallei and characterized by ulceration of the respiratory mucosa and an eruption of nodules on the skin.','en','1','2007-10-18 04:28:24','1',NULL,'12289FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF');
REPLACE INTO `concept_description` (`concept_description_id`, `concept_id`, `description`, `locale`, `creator`, `date_created`, `changed_by`, `date_changed`, `uuid`) values('12290','139439','Disease of the gums.','en','1','2007-10-18 04:28:24','1',NULL,'12290FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF');
REPLACE INTO `concept_description` (`concept_description_id`, `concept_id`, `description`, `locale`, `creator`, `date_created`, `changed_by`, `date_changed`, `uuid`) values('12291','139442','Generalized or localized diffuse fibrous overgrowth of the gingival tissue, usually transmitted as an autosomal dominant trait, but some cases are idiopathic and others produced by drugs. The enlarged gingiva is pink, firm, and has a leather-like consistency with a minutely pebbled surface and in severe cases the teeth are almost completely covered and the enlargement projects into the oral vestibule. (Dorland, 28th ed)','en','1','2007-10-18 04:28:24','1',NULL,'12291FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF');
REPLACE INTO `concept_description` (`concept_description_id`, `concept_id`, `description`, `locale`, `creator`, `date_created`, `changed_by`, `date_changed`, `uuid`) values('12292','139443','Non-inflammatory enlargement of the gingivae produced by factors other than local irritation. It is characteristically due to an increase in the number of cells. (From Jablonski\'s Dictionary of Dentistry, 1992, p400)','en','1','2007-10-18 04:28:24','1',NULL,'12292FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF');
REPLACE INTO `concept_description` (`concept_description_id`, `concept_id`, `description`, `locale`, `creator`, `date_created`, `changed_by`, `date_changed`, `uuid`) values('12293','139446','Disease of the gums.','en','1','2007-10-18 04:28:24','1',NULL,'12293FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF');
REPLACE INTO `concept_description` (`concept_description_id`, `concept_id`, `description`, `locale`, `creator`, `date_created`, `changed_by`, `date_changed`, `uuid`) values('12294','139447','A group of conditions of diverse etiologies characterized by the accumulation of insoluble fibrillar proteins (amyloid) in various organs and tissues of the body such that vital function is compromised. The associated disease states may be inflammatory, hereditary, or neoplastic, and the deposition can be localized or generalized or systemic. (Dorland, 27th ed)','en','1','2007-10-18 04:28:24','1',NULL,'12294FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF');
REPLACE INTO `concept_description` (`concept_description_id`, `concept_id`, `description`, `locale`, `creator`, `date_created`, `changed_by`, `date_changed`, `uuid`) values('12295','139448','Disorders characterized by recurrent TICS that may interfere with speech and other activities. Tics are sudden, rapid, nonrhythmic, stereotyped motor movements or vocalizations which may be exacerbated by stress and are generally attenuated during absorbing activities. Tic disorders are distinguished from conditions which feature other types of abnormal movements that may accompany general medical conditions. (From DSM-IV, 1994)','en','1','2007-10-18 04:28:24','1',NULL,'12295FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF');
REPLACE INTO `concept_description` (`concept_description_id`, `concept_id`, `description`, `locale`, `creator`, `date_created`, `changed_by`, `date_changed`, `uuid`) values('12297','139450','A benign familial disorder, transmitted as an autosomal dominant trait. It is characterized by low-grade chronic hyperbilirubinemia with considerable daily fluctuations of the bilirubin level.','en','1','2007-10-18 04:28:24','1',NULL,'12297FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF');
REPLACE INTO `concept_description` (`concept_description_id`, `concept_id`, `description`, `locale`, `creator`, `date_created`, `changed_by`, `date_changed`, `uuid`) values('12298','139454','The condition of abnormal overgrowth or excessive size of the whole body or any of its parts.','en','1','2007-10-18 04:28:24','1',NULL,'12298FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF');
REPLACE INTO `concept_description` (`concept_description_id`, `concept_id`, `description`, `locale`, `creator`, `date_created`, `changed_by`, `date_changed`, `uuid`) values('12299','139456','Impairment in the comprehension of speech and meaning of words, both spoken and written, and of the meanings conveyed by their grammatical relationships in sentences. It is caused by lesions that primarily affect Wernicke\'s area, which lies in the posterior perisylvian region of the temporal lobe of the dominant hemisphere. (From Brain & Bannister, Clinical Neurology, 7th ed, p141; Kandel et al., Principles of Neural Science, 3d ed, p846)','en','1','2007-10-18 04:28:24','1',NULL,'12299FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF');
REPLACE INTO `concept_description` (`concept_description_id`, `concept_id`, `description`, `locale`, `creator`, `date_created`, `changed_by`, `date_changed`, `uuid`) values('12300','139457','An infection of the small intestine caused by the flagellated protozoan GIARDIA LAMBLIA. It is spread via contaminated food and water and by direct person-to-person contact.','en','1','2007-10-18 04:28:24','1',NULL,'12300FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF');
REPLACE INTO `concept_description` (`concept_description_id`, `concept_id`, `description`, `locale`, `creator`, `date_created`, `changed_by`, `date_changed`, `uuid`) values('12301','139458','Recurring attacks of transient edema suddenly appearing in areas of the skin or mucous membranes and occasionally of the viscera, often associated with dermatographism, urticaria, erythema, and purpura.','en','1','2007-10-18 04:28:24','1',NULL,'12301FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF');
REPLACE INTO `concept_description` (`concept_description_id`, `concept_id`, `description`, `locale`, `creator`, `date_created`, `changed_by`, `date_changed`, `uuid`) values('12302','139459','A familial coagulation disorder characterized by a prolonged bleeding time, unusually large platelets, and impaired prothrombin consumption.','en','1','2007-10-18 04:28:24','1',NULL,'12302FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF');
REPLACE INTO `concept_description` (`concept_description_id`, `concept_id`, `description`, `locale`, `creator`, `date_created`, `changed_by`, `date_changed`, `uuid`) values('12303','139460','Conjunctivitis due to hypersensitivity to various allergens.','en','1','2007-10-18 04:28:24','1',NULL,'12303FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF');
REPLACE INTO `concept_description` (`concept_description_id`, `concept_id`, `description`, `locale`, `creator`, `date_created`, `changed_by`, `date_changed`, `uuid`) values('12304','139461','Large benign, hyperplastic lymph nodes. The more common hyaline vascular subtype is characterized by small hyaline vascular follicles and interfollicular capillary proliferations. Plasma cells are often present and represent another subtype with the plasma cells containing IgM and IgA.','en','1','2007-10-18 04:28:24','1',NULL,'12304FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF');
REPLACE INTO `concept_description` (`concept_description_id`, `concept_id`, `description`, `locale`, `creator`, `date_created`, `changed_by`, `date_changed`, `uuid`) values('12305','139468','Pneumonia caused by a virus. (Dorland, 28th ed)','en','1','2007-10-18 04:28:24','1',NULL,'12305FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF');
REPLACE INTO `concept_description` (`concept_description_id`, `concept_id`, `description`, `locale`, `creator`, `date_created`, `changed_by`, `date_changed`, `uuid`) values('12306','139470','A non-neoplastic inflammatory lesion, usually of the jaw or gingiva, containing large, multinucleated cells. It includes reparative giant cell granuloma. Peripheral giant cell granuloma refers to the gingiva (giant cell epulis); central refers to the jaw.','en','1','2007-10-18 04:28:24','1',NULL,'12306FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF');
REPLACE INTO `concept_description` (`concept_description_id`, `concept_id`, `description`, `locale`, `creator`, `date_created`, `changed_by`, `date_changed`, `uuid`) values('12307','139471','A non-neoplastic inflammatory lesion, usually of the jaw or gingiva, containing large, multinucleated cells. It includes reparative giant cell granuloma. Peripheral giant cell granuloma refers to the gingiva (giant cell epulis); central refers to the jaw.','en','1','2007-10-18 04:28:24','1',NULL,'12307FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF');
REPLACE INTO `concept_description` (`concept_description_id`, `concept_id`, `description`, `locale`, `creator`, `date_created`, `changed_by`, `date_changed`, `uuid`) values('12308','139472','A systemic autoimmune vasculitis occurring primarily in people over the age of 50. Pathologic features include a necrotizing panarteritis including granulomas and giant cells. There is a predilection for involvement of central nervous system blood vessels and the most frequent neurologic complication is an OPTIC NEUROPATHY, ISCHEMIC. Large blood vessels may become involved, including the aorta. Clinical manifestations may include myalgias, weight loss, headache, visual loss, necrosis of the skin or tongue, and chest discomfort. Superficial scalp arteries may become tender and enlarged. A related condition, juvenile temporal arteritis, tends to occur in the first or second decade of life. (From Adams et al., Principles of Neurology, 6th ed, p856)','en','1','2007-10-18 04:28:24','1',NULL,'12308FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF');
REPLACE INTO `concept_description` (`concept_description_id`, `concept_id`, `description`, `locale`, `creator`, `date_created`, `changed_by`, `date_changed`, `uuid`) values('12309','139474','Maladaptive reactions to identifiable psychosocial stressors occurring within a short time after onset of the stressor. They are manifested by either impairment in social or occupational functioning or by symptoms (depression, anxiety, etc.) that are in excess of a normal and expected reaction to the stressor.','en','1','2007-10-18 04:28:24','1',NULL,'12309FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF');
REPLACE INTO `concept_description` (`concept_description_id`, `concept_id`, `description`, `locale`, `creator`, `date_created`, `changed_by`, `date_changed`, `uuid`) values('12311','139476','A group of cognitive disorders characterized by the inability to perform previously learned skills that cannot be attributed to deficits of motor or sensory function. The two major subtypes of this condition are ideomotor (see APRAXIA, IDEOMOTOR) and ideational apraxia, which refers to loss of the ability to mentally formulate the processes involved with performing an action. For example, dressing apraxia may result from an inability to mentally formulate the act of placing clothes on the body. Apraxias are generally associated with lesions of the dominant PARIETAL LOBE and supramarginal gyrus. (From Adams et al., Principles of Neurology, 6th ed, pp56-7)','en','1','2007-10-18 04:28:24','1',NULL,'12311FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF');
REPLACE INTO `concept_description` (`concept_description_id`, `concept_id`, `description`, `locale`, `creator`, `date_created`, `changed_by`, `date_changed`, `uuid`) values('12312','139477','A trophoblastic disease characterized by hydrops of the mesenchymal portion of the villus. Its karyotype is paternal and usually homozygotic. The tumor is indistinguishable from chorioadenoma destruens or invasive mole ( = HYDATIDIFORM MOLE, INVASIVE) except by karyotype. There is no apparent relation by karyotype to CHORIOCARCINOMA. Hydatidiform refers to the presence of the hydropic state of some or all of the villi (Greek hydatis, a drop of water).','en','1','2007-10-18 04:28:24','1',NULL,'12312FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF');
REPLACE INTO `concept_description` (`concept_description_id`, `concept_id`, `description`, `locale`, `creator`, `date_created`, `changed_by`, `date_changed`, `uuid`) values('12313','139478','A trophoblastic disease characterized by hydrops of the mesenchymal portion of the villus. Its karyotype is paternal and usually homozygotic. The tumor is indistinguishable from chorioadenoma destruens or invasive mole ( = HYDATIDIFORM MOLE, INVASIVE) except by karyotype. There is no apparent relation by karyotype to CHORIOCARCINOMA. Hydatidiform refers to the presence of the hydropic state of some or all of the villi (Greek hydatis, a drop of water).','en','1','2007-10-18 04:28:24','1',NULL,'12313FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF');
REPLACE INTO `concept_description` (`concept_description_id`, `concept_id`, `description`, `locale`, `creator`, `date_created`, `changed_by`, `date_changed`, `uuid`) values('12314','139479','Transplacental infection of the fetus with rubella usually in the first trimester of pregnancy, as a consequence of maternal infection, resulting in various developmental abnormalities in the newborn infant. They include cardiac and ocular lesions, deafness, microcephaly, mental retardation, and generalized growth retardation. (From Dorland, 27th ed)','en','1','2007-10-18 04:28:24','1',NULL,'12314FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF');
REPLACE INTO `concept_description` (`concept_description_id`, `concept_id`, `description`, `locale`, `creator`, `date_created`, `changed_by`, `date_changed`, `uuid`) values('12316','139493','Infection due to the fungus Geotrichum.','en','1','2007-10-18 04:28:24','1',NULL,'12316FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF');
REPLACE INTO `concept_description` (`concept_description_id`, `concept_id`, `description`, `locale`, `creator`, `date_created`, `changed_by`, `date_changed`, `uuid`) values('12317','139494','The persistent eating of nonnutritive substances for a period of at least one month. (DSM-IV)','en','1','2007-10-18 04:28:24','1',NULL,'12317FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF');
REPLACE INTO `concept_description` (`concept_description_id`, `concept_id`, `description`, `locale`, `creator`, `date_created`, `changed_by`, `date_changed`, `uuid`) values('12318','139495','An idiopathic disorder characterized by the loss of filiform papillae leaving reddened areas of circinate macules bound by a white band. The lesions heal, then others erupt.','en','1','2007-10-18 04:28:24','1',NULL,'12318FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF');
REPLACE INTO `concept_description` (`concept_description_id`, `concept_id`, `description`, `locale`, `creator`, `date_created`, `changed_by`, `date_changed`, `uuid`) values('12319','139497','Diseases of the skin with a genetic component, usually the result of various inborn errors of metabolism.','en','1','2007-10-18 04:28:24','1',NULL,'12319FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF');
REPLACE INTO `concept_description` (`concept_description_id`, `concept_id`, `description`, `locale`, `creator`, `date_created`, `changed_by`, `date_changed`, `uuid`) values('12320','139503','The invasion of living tissues of man and other mammals by dipterous larvae.','en','1','2007-10-18 04:28:24','1',NULL,'12320FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF');
REPLACE INTO `concept_description` (`concept_description_id`, `concept_id`, `description`, `locale`, `creator`, `date_created`, `changed_by`, `date_changed`, `uuid`) values('12321','139505','Sexually transmitted form of anogenital warty growth caused by the human papillomaviruses.','en','1','2007-10-18 04:28:24','1',NULL,'12321FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF');
REPLACE INTO `concept_description` (`concept_description_id`, `concept_id`, `description`, `locale`, `creator`, `date_created`, `changed_by`, `date_changed`, `uuid`) values('12322','139510','Invasion and multiplication of microorganisms in body tissues, which may be clinically inapparent or result in local cellular injury. A local infection may persist and spread by extension to become an acute, subacute, or chronic clinical infection or disease state. It may also become systemic when the microorganisms gain access to the lymphatic or vascular system. (From Dorland, 27th ed)','en','1','2007-10-18 04:28:24','1',NULL,'12322FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF');
REPLACE INTO `concept_description` (`concept_description_id`, `concept_id`, `description`, `locale`, `creator`, `date_created`, `changed_by`, `date_changed`, `uuid`) values('12323','139511','The occurrence in an individual of two or more cell populations of different chromosomal constitutions, derived from a single zygote.','en','1','2007-10-18 04:28:24','1',NULL,'12323FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF');
REPLACE INTO `concept_description` (`concept_description_id`, `concept_id`, `description`, `locale`, `creator`, `date_created`, `changed_by`, `date_changed`, `uuid`) values('12324','139512','A disturbance of lipid metabolism with abnormal deposit of lipids in the cells. (Dorland, 27th ed)','en','1','2007-10-18 04:28:24','1',NULL,'12324FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF');
REPLACE INTO `concept_description` (`concept_description_id`, `concept_id`, `description`, `locale`, `creator`, `date_created`, `changed_by`, `date_changed`, `uuid`) values('12325','139513','An inherited defect interfering with normal nuclear lobulation of neutrophils and eosinophils. The nuclei appear rodlike, spherical, or dumbbell-shaped and their structure is coarse and lumpy. (From Dorland, 27th ed)','en','1','2007-10-18 04:28:24','1',NULL,'12325FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF');
REPLACE INTO `concept_description` (`concept_description_id`, `concept_id`, `description`, `locale`, `creator`, `date_created`, `changed_by`, `date_changed`, `uuid`) values('12326','139519','An acute form of TUBERCULOSIS in which minute tubercles are formed in a number of organs of the body due to dissemination of the bacilli through the blood stream.','en','1','2007-10-18 04:28:24','1',NULL,'12326FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF');
REPLACE INTO `concept_description` (`concept_description_id`, `concept_id`, `description`, `locale`, `creator`, `date_created`, `changed_by`, `date_changed`, `uuid`) values('12327','139520','An inherited syndrome of peripheral resistance to thyroid hormones, transmitted as an autosomal recessive trait, characterized by increased serum concentrations of thyroxine and triiodothyronine, increased thyroid hormone binding ratio, and normal to slightly increased thyroid-stimulating hormone and its response to thyrotropin-releasing hormone. The affected persons are euthyroid to slightly hypothyroid. The absence of hypermetabolism and the presence of possible hypothyroidism indicate the existence of partial resistance to the peripheral action of thyroid hormone. (From Jablonski\'s Dictionary of syndromes & eponymic diseases, 1991)','en','1','2007-10-18 04:28:24','1',NULL,'12327FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF');
REPLACE INTO `concept_description` (`concept_description_id`, `concept_id`, `description`, `locale`, `creator`, `date_created`, `changed_by`, `date_changed`, `uuid`) values('12328','139521','Anxiety disorders in which the essential feature is persistent and irrational fear of a specific object, activity, or situation that the individual feels compelled to avoid. The individual recognizes the fear as excessive or unreasonable.','en','1','2007-10-18 04:28:24','1','2016-07-01 16:30:35','12328FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF');
REPLACE INTO `concept_description` (`concept_description_id`, `concept_id`, `description`, `locale`, `creator`, `date_created`, `changed_by`, `date_changed`, `uuid`) values('12329','139527','A mental disorder characterized by chronic fatigue and concomitant physiologic symptoms.','en','1','2007-10-18 04:28:24','1',NULL,'12329FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF');
REPLACE INTO `concept_description` (`concept_description_id`, `concept_id`, `description`, `locale`, `creator`, `date_created`, `changed_by`, `date_changed`, `uuid`) values('12330','139528','Generic term for diseases caused by an abnormal metabolic process. It can be congenital due to inherited enzyme abnormality (METABOLISM, INBORN ERRORS) or acquired due to disease of an endocrine organ or failure of a metabolically important organ such as the liver. (Stedman, 26th ed)','en','1','2007-10-18 04:28:24','1',NULL,'12330FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF');
REPLACE INTO `concept_description` (`concept_description_id`, `concept_id`, `description`, `locale`, `creator`, `date_created`, `changed_by`, `date_changed`, `uuid`) values('12331','139529','A disorder of cardiac function caused by insufficient blood flow to the muscle tissue of the heart. The decreased blood flow may be due to narrowing of the coronary arteries (CORONARY ARTERIOSCLEROSIS), to obstruction by a thrombus (CORONARY THROMBOSIS), or less commonly, to diffuse narrowing of arterioles and other small vessels within the heart. Severe interruption of the blood supply to the myocardial tissue may result in necrosis of cardiac muscle (MYOCARDIAL INFARCTION).','en','1','2007-10-18 04:28:24','1',NULL,'12331FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF');
REPLACE INTO `concept_description` (`concept_description_id`, `concept_id`, `description`, `locale`, `creator`, `date_created`, `changed_by`, `date_changed`, `uuid`) values('12332','139534','Pain in the cranial region that may occur as an isolated and benign symptom or as a manifestation of a wide variety of conditions including SUBARACHNOID HEMORRHAGE; CRANIOCEREBRAL TRAUMA; CENTRAL NERVOUS SYSTEM INFECTIONS; INTRACRANIAL HYPERTENSION; and other disorders. In general, recurrent headaches that are not associated with a primary disease process are referred to as HEADACHE DISORDERS (e.g., MIGRAINE).','en','1','2007-10-18 04:28:24','1',NULL,'12332FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF');
REPLACE INTO `concept_description` (`concept_description_id`, `concept_id`, `description`, `locale`, `creator`, `date_created`, `changed_by`, `date_changed`, `uuid`) values('12333','139535','A group of inherited metabolic disorders involving the enzymes responsible for the synthesis and degradation of glycogen. In some patients, prominent liver involvement is presented. In others, more generalized storage of glycogen occurs, sometimes with prominent cardiac involvement.','en','1','2007-10-18 04:28:24','1',NULL,'12333FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF');
REPLACE INTO `concept_description` (`concept_description_id`, `concept_id`, `description`, `locale`, `creator`, `date_created`, `changed_by`, `date_changed`, `uuid`) values('12334','139537','The exposure of root surface by an apical shift in the position of the gingiva.','en','1','2007-10-18 04:28:24','1',NULL,'12334FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF');
REPLACE INTO `concept_description` (`concept_description_id`, `concept_id`, `description`, `locale`, `creator`, `date_created`, `changed_by`, `date_changed`, `uuid`) values('12335','139540','Form of epidermolysis bullosa characterized by autosomal dominant inheritance and by serous bullae that heal without scarring.','en','1','2007-10-18 04:28:24','1',NULL,'12335FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF');
REPLACE INTO `concept_description` (`concept_description_id`, `concept_id`, `description`, `locale`, `creator`, `date_created`, `changed_by`, `date_changed`, `uuid`) values('12336','139544','Rare chronic inflammatory disease involving the small blood vessels. It is of unknown etiology and characterized by mucocutaneous ulceration in the mouth and genital region and uveitis with hypopyon. The neuro-ocular form may cause blindness and death. Synovitis, thrombophlebitis, gastrointestinal ulcerations, retinal vasculitis, and optic atrophy may be occur as well.','en','1','2007-10-18 04:28:24','1',NULL,'12336FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF');
REPLACE INTO `concept_description` (`concept_description_id`, `concept_id`, `description`, `locale`, `creator`, `date_created`, `changed_by`, `date_changed`, `uuid`) values('12337','139545','Disorders in which anxiety (persistent feelings of apprehension, tension, or uneasiness) is the predominant disturbance.','en','1','2007-10-18 04:28:24','1','2016-07-01 16:34:21','12337FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF');
REPLACE INTO `concept_description` (`concept_description_id`, `concept_id`, `description`, `locale`, `creator`, `date_created`, `changed_by`, `date_changed`, `uuid`) values('12338','139547','Sensation of discomfort, distress, or agony in the abdominal region.','en','1','2007-10-18 04:28:24','1','2015-12-31 16:25:05','12338FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF');
REPLACE INTO `concept_description` (`concept_description_id`, `concept_id`, `description`, `locale`, `creator`, `date_created`, `changed_by`, `date_changed`, `uuid`) values('12339','139565','Continuous involuntary sustained muscle contraction which is often a manifestation of BASAL GANGLIA DISEASES. When an affected muscle is passively stretched, the degree of resistance remains constant regardless of the rate at which the muscle is stretched. This feature helps to distinguish rigidity from MUSCLE SPASTICITY. (From Adams et al., Principles of Neurology, 6th ed, p73)','en','1','2007-10-18 04:28:24','1','2016-02-08 02:33:22','12339FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF');
REPLACE INTO `concept_description` (`concept_description_id`, `concept_id`, `description`, `locale`, `creator`, `date_created`, `changed_by`, `date_changed`, `uuid`) values('12340','139566','A disturbance of lipid metabolism with abnormal deposit of lipids in the cells. (Dorland, 27th ed)','en','1','2007-10-18 04:28:24','1',NULL,'12340FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF');
REPLACE INTO `concept_description` (`concept_description_id`, `concept_id`, `description`, `locale`, `creator`, `date_created`, `changed_by`, `date_changed`, `uuid`) values('12341','139569','A congenital fissure of the abdominal wall not involving the site of insertion of the umbilical cord, and usually accompanied by protrusion of the small and part of the large intestine. (Dorland, 28th ed)','en','1','2007-10-18 04:28:24','1',NULL,'12341FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF');
REPLACE INTO `concept_description` (`concept_description_id`, `concept_id`, `description`, `locale`, `creator`, `date_created`, `changed_by`, `date_changed`, `uuid`) values('12342','139575','Bleeding in the gastrointestinal tract.','en','1','2007-10-18 04:28:24','1','2012-11-02 22:53:47','12342FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF');
REPLACE INTO `concept_description` (`concept_description_id`, `concept_id`, `description`, `locale`, `creator`, `date_created`, `changed_by`, `date_changed`, `uuid`) values('12343','139579','Any impairment, arrest, or reversal of the normal flow of intestinal contents toward the anus.','en','1','2007-10-18 04:28:24','1',NULL,'12343FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF');
REPLACE INTO `concept_description` (`concept_description_id`, `concept_id`, `description`, `locale`, `creator`, `date_created`, `changed_by`, `date_changed`, `uuid`) values('12344','139582','Bleeding in the gastrointestinal tract.','en','1','2007-10-18 04:28:24','1','2015-11-03 02:58:44','12344FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF');
REPLACE INTO `concept_description` (`concept_description_id`, `concept_id`, `description`, `locale`, `creator`, `date_created`, `changed_by`, `date_changed`, `uuid`) values('12345','139587','Infection with a fungus of the genus CANDIDA. It is usually a superficial infection of the moist areas of the body and is generally caused by CANDIDA ALBICANS. (Dorland, 27th ed)','en','1','2007-10-18 04:28:24','1',NULL,'12345FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF');
REPLACE INTO `concept_description` (`concept_description_id`, `concept_id`, `description`, `locale`, `creator`, `date_created`, `changed_by`, `date_changed`, `uuid`) values('12346','139588','An acute bacterial infection caused by ingestion of BACILLUS organisms. Carnivores may become infected from ingestion of infected carcasses. It is transmitted to humans by contact with infected animals or contaminated animal products. The most common form in humans is cutaneous anthrax.','en','1','2007-10-18 04:28:24','1',NULL,'12346FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF');
REPLACE INTO `concept_description` (`concept_description_id`, `concept_id`, `description`, `locale`, `creator`, `date_created`, `changed_by`, `date_changed`, `uuid`) values('12347','139590','Inflammation of the esophagus caused by reflux of gastric juice and/or stomach and duodenal contents.','en','1','2007-10-18 04:28:24','1','2012-06-26 00:44:46','12347FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF');
REPLACE INTO `concept_description` (`concept_description_id`, `concept_id`, `description`, `locale`, `creator`, `date_created`, `changed_by`, `date_changed`, `uuid`) values('12348','139591','Inflammation of the lining of the stomach and intestines, often accompanied by diarrhea.','en','1','2007-10-18 04:28:24','1',NULL,'12348FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF');
REPLACE INTO `concept_description` (`concept_description_id`, `concept_id`, `description`, `locale`, `creator`, `date_created`, `changed_by`, `date_changed`, `uuid`) values('12349','139598','A gastrin-secreting tumor of the non-beta islet cells. It is usually located in the pancreas but is also found at other sites, as in the antrum of the stomach, hilus of the spleen, and regional lymph nodes. The presence of gastrinoma is one of three requirements to be met for identification of ZOLLINGER-ELLISON SYNDROME, which sometimes occurs in families with MULTIPLE ENDOCRINE NEOPLASIA TYPE 1 (MEN-1). Gastrinomas in patients with MEN-1 are usually diffuse in nature.','en','1','2007-10-18 04:28:24','1',NULL,'12349FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF');
REPLACE INTO `concept_description` (`concept_description_id`, `concept_id`, `description`, `locale`, `creator`, `date_created`, `changed_by`, `date_changed`, `uuid`) values('12350','139599','Twisting of the stomach that may result in obstruction and impairment of the blood supply to the organ. It can occur in paraesophageal hernia and occasionally in eventration of the diaphragm. (Stedman, 25th ed)','en','1','2007-10-18 04:28:24','1',NULL,'12350FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF');
REPLACE INTO `concept_description` (`concept_description_id`, `concept_id`, `description`, `locale`, `creator`, `date_created`, `changed_by`, `date_changed`, `uuid`) values('12351','139600','Submucosal varices of the lower esophagus or gastric fundus mucosa, frequently caused by the development of portal collateral vessels consequent to portal hypertension.','en','1','2007-10-18 04:28:24','1',NULL,'12351FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF');
REPLACE INTO `concept_description` (`concept_description_id`, `concept_id`, `description`, `locale`, `creator`, `date_created`, `changed_by`, `date_changed`, `uuid`) values('12352','139605','Bleeding from a peptic ulcer.','en','1','2007-10-18 04:28:24','1',NULL,'12352FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF');
REPLACE INTO `concept_description` (`concept_description_id`, `concept_id`, `description`, `locale`, `creator`, `date_created`, `changed_by`, `date_changed`, `uuid`) values('12353','139610','Reflux of gastric juice and/or duodenal contents (bile acids, pancreatic juice) into the distal esophagus, commonly due to incompetence of the lower esophageal sphincter. Gastric regurgitation is an extension of this process with entry of fluid into the pharynx or mouth.','en','1','2007-10-18 04:28:24','1',NULL,'12353FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF');
REPLACE INTO `concept_description` (`concept_description_id`, `concept_id`, `description`, `locale`, `creator`, `date_created`, `changed_by`, `date_changed`, `uuid`) values('12354','139614','Bleeding in the gastrointestinal tract.','en','1','2007-10-18 04:28:24','1',NULL,'12354FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF');
REPLACE INTO `concept_description` (`concept_description_id`, `concept_id`, `description`, `locale`, `creator`, `date_created`, `changed_by`, `date_changed`, `uuid`) values('12355','139615','Abnormal passage communicating with the stomach.','en','1','2007-10-18 04:28:24','1',NULL,'12355FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF');
REPLACE INTO `concept_description` (`concept_description_id`, `concept_id`, `description`, `locale`, `creator`, `date_created`, `changed_by`, `date_changed`, `uuid`) values('12356','139619','Saccular, outward protrusion of a portion of the mucous membrane of the stomach wall.','en','1','2007-10-18 04:28:24','1',NULL,'12356FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF');
REPLACE INTO `concept_description` (`concept_description_id`, `concept_id`, `description`, `locale`, `creator`, `date_created`, `changed_by`, `date_changed`, `uuid`) values('12357','139623','The prolapse of one part of the intestine into the lumen of an immediately adjoining part. There are four varieties: colic, involving segments of the large intestine; enteric, involving only the small intestine; ileocecal, in which the ileocecal valve prolapses into the cecum, drawing the ileum along with it; and ileocolic, in which the ileum prolapses through the ileocecal valve into the colon. (Dorland, 27th ed)','en','1','2007-10-18 04:28:24','1',NULL,'12357FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF');
REPLACE INTO `concept_description` (`concept_description_id`, `concept_id`, `description`, `locale`, `creator`, `date_created`, `changed_by`, `date_changed`, `uuid`) values('12358','139625','A severe condition resulting from bacteria invading healthy muscle from adjacent traumatized muscle or soft tissue. The infection originates in a wound contaminated with bacteria of the genus CLOSTRIDIUM. C. perfringens accounts for the majority of cases (over eighty percent), while C. noyvi, C. septicum, and C. histolyticum cause most of the other cases.','en','1','2007-10-18 04:28:24','1',NULL,'12358FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF');
REPLACE INTO `concept_description` (`concept_description_id`, `concept_id`, `description`, `locale`, `creator`, `date_created`, `changed_by`, `date_changed`, `uuid`) values('12359','139626','A severe condition resulting from bacteria invading healthy muscle from adjacent traumatized muscle or soft tissue. The infection originates in a wound contaminated with bacteria of the genus CLOSTRIDIUM. C. perfringens accounts for the majority of cases (over eighty percent), while C. noyvi, C. septicum, and C. histolyticum cause most of the other cases.','en','1','2007-10-18 04:28:24','1',NULL,'12359FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF');
