REPLACE INTO `concept_description` (`concept_description_id`, `concept_id`, `description`, `locale`, `creator`, `date_created`, `changed_by`, `date_changed`, `uuid`) values('12588','140471','An abnormal elevation of body temperature, usually as a result of a pathologic process.','en','1','2007-10-18 04:28:24','1','2020-03-16 18:59:50','12588FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF');
REPLACE INTO `concept_description` (`concept_description_id`, `concept_id`, `description`, `locale`, `creator`, `date_created`, `changed_by`, `date_changed`, `uuid`) values('12589','140472','An affective disorder manifested by either a dysphoric mood or loss of interest or pleasure in usual activities. The mood disturbance is prominent and relatively persistent.','en','1','2007-10-18 04:28:24','1','2016-07-01 16:19:02','12589FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF');
REPLACE INTO `concept_description` (`concept_description_id`, `concept_id`, `description`, `locale`, `creator`, `date_created`, `changed_by`, `date_changed`, `uuid`) values('12590','140485','Seizures that occur during a febrile episode. It is a common condition, affecting 2-5% of children aged 3 months to five years. An autosomal dominant pattern of inheritance has been identified in some families. The majority are simple febrile seizures (generally defined as generalized onset, single seizures with a duration of less than 30 minutes). Complex febrile seizures are characterized by focal onset, duration greater than 30 minutes, and/or more than one seizure in a 24 hour period. The likelihood of developing epilepsy (i.e., a nonfebrile seizure disorder) following simple febrile seizures is low. Complex febrile seizures are associated with a moderately increased incidence of epilepsy. (From Menkes, Textbook of Child Neurology, 5th ed, p784)','en','1','2007-10-18 04:28:24','1','2016-05-25 20:33:11','12590FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF');
REPLACE INTO `concept_description` (`concept_description_id`, `concept_id`, `description`, `locale`, `creator`, `date_created`, `changed_by`, `date_changed`, `uuid`) values('12591','140487','Anxiety disorders in which the essential feature is persistent and irrational fear of a specific object, activity, or situation that the individual feels compelled to avoid. The individual recognizes the fear as excessive or unreasonable.','en','1','2007-10-18 04:28:24','1','2016-07-01 16:17:41','12591FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF');
REPLACE INTO `concept_description` (`concept_description_id`, `concept_id`, `description`, `locale`, `creator`, `date_created`, `changed_by`, `date_changed`, `uuid`) values('12592','140488','Anxiety disorders in which the essential feature is persistent and irrational fear of a specific object, activity, or situation that the individual feels compelled to avoid. The individual recognizes the fear as excessive or unreasonable.','en','1','2007-10-18 04:28:24','1',NULL,'12592FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF');
REPLACE INTO `concept_description` (`concept_description_id`, `concept_id`, `description`, `locale`, `creator`, `date_created`, `changed_by`, `date_changed`, `uuid`) values('12593','140492','Anxiety disorders in which the essential feature is persistent and irrational fear of a specific object, activity, or situation that the individual feels compelled to avoid. The individual recognizes the fear as excessive or unreasonable.','en','1','2007-10-18 04:28:24','1',NULL,'12593FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF');
REPLACE INTO `concept_description` (`concept_description_id`, `concept_id`, `description`, `locale`, `creator`, `date_created`, `changed_by`, `date_changed`, `uuid`) values('12595','140495','Hemolytic anemia due to the ingestion of fava beans or after inhalation of pollen from the Vicia fava plant by persons with glucose-6-phosphate dehydrogenase deficient erythrocytes.','en','1','2007-10-18 04:28:24','1',NULL,'12595FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF');
REPLACE INTO `concept_description` (`concept_description_id`, `concept_id`, `description`, `locale`, `creator`, `date_created`, `changed_by`, `date_changed`, `uuid`) values('12596','140496','A common congenital midline defect of fusion of the vertebral arch without protrusion of the spinal cord or meninges. The lesion is also covered by skin. L5 and S1 are the most common vertebrae involved. The condition may be associated with an overlying area of hyperpigmented skin, a dermal sinus, or an abnormal patch of hair. The majority of individuals with this malformation are asymptomatic although there is an increased incidence of tethered cord syndrome and lumbar SPONDYLOSIS. (From Joynt, Clinical Neurology, 1992, Ch55, p34)','en','1','2007-10-18 04:28:24','1',NULL,'12596FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF');
REPLACE INTO `concept_description` (`concept_description_id`, `concept_id`, `description`, `locale`, `creator`, `date_created`, `changed_by`, `date_changed`, `uuid`) values('12597','140497','A localized infection of mucous membranes or skin caused by toxigenic strains of CORYNEBACTERIUM DIPHTHERIAE. It is characterized by the presence of a pseudomembrane at the site of infection. DIPHTHERIA TOXIN, produced by C. diphtheriae, can cause myocarditis, polyneuritis, and other systemic toxic effects.','en','1','2007-10-18 04:28:24','1',NULL,'12597FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF');
REPLACE INTO `concept_description` (`concept_description_id`, `concept_id`, `description`, `locale`, `creator`, `date_created`, `changed_by`, `date_changed`, `uuid`) values('12598','140498','Yellow discoloration of the liver due to fatty degeneration of liver parenchymal cells. (Stedman, 25th ed)','en','1','2007-10-18 04:28:24','1',NULL,'12598FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF');
REPLACE INTO `concept_description` (`concept_description_id`, `concept_id`, `description`, `locale`, `creator`, `date_created`, `changed_by`, `date_changed`, `uuid`) values('12599','140502','Involuntary movements of the eye that are divided into two types, jerk and pendular. Jerk nystagmus has a slow phase in one direction followed by a corrective fast phase in the opposite direction, and is usually caused by central or peripheral vestibular dysfunction. Pendular nystagmus features oscillations that are of equal velocity in both directions and this condition is often associated with visual loss early in life. (Adams et al., Principles of Neurology, 6th ed, p272)','en','1','2007-10-18 04:28:24','1',NULL,'12599FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF');
REPLACE INTO `concept_description` (`concept_description_id`, `concept_id`, `description`, `locale`, `creator`, `date_created`, `changed_by`, `date_changed`, `uuid`) values('12600','140503','A group of genetic, infectious, or sporadic degenerative human and animal nervous system disorders associated with abnormal PRIONS. These diseases are characterized by conversion of the normal prion protein to an abnormal configuration via a post-translational process. In humans, these conditions generally feature DEMENTIA, ataxia, and a fatal outcome. Diseases in this category include CREUTZFELDT-JAKOB SYNDROME; GERSTMANN-STRAUSSLER-SCHEINKER SYNDROME; KURU; SCRAPIE; fatal familial insomnia; bovine spongiform encephalopathy (see ENCEPHALOPATHY, BOVINE SPONGIFORM); transmissible mink encephalopathy; and chronic wasting disease of mule deer and elk. Pathologic features include a spongiform encephalopathy without evidence of inflammation. The literature occasionally refers to these as unconventional SLOW VIRUS DISEASES. (From Proc Natl Acad Sci USA 1998 Nov 10;95(23):13363-83)','en','1','2007-10-18 04:28:24','1',NULL,'12600FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF');
REPLACE INTO `concept_description` (`concept_description_id`, `concept_id`, `description`, `locale`, `creator`, `date_created`, `changed_by`, `date_changed`, `uuid`) values('12602','140510','Embolism caused by fat entering the circulation. It is often seen after fractures of large bones or after corticosteriod administration.','en','1','2007-10-18 04:28:24','1',NULL,'12602FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF');
REPLACE INTO `concept_description` (`concept_description_id`, `concept_id`, `description`, `locale`, `creator`, `date_created`, `changed_by`, `date_changed`, `uuid`) values('12604','140512','An abnormally diminished concentration of glucose in the blood, which may lead to tremulousness, cold sweat, piloerection, hypothermia, and headache, accompanied by irritability, confusion, hallucinations, bizarre behavior, and ultimately, convulsions and coma. (Dorland, 27th ed)','en','1','2007-10-18 04:28:24','1',NULL,'12604FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF');
REPLACE INTO `concept_description` (`concept_description_id`, `concept_id`, `description`, `locale`, `creator`, `date_created`, `changed_by`, `date_changed`, `uuid`) values('12605','140513','Helminth infection of the liver caused by species of Fasciola.','en','1','2007-10-18 04:28:24','1',NULL,'12605FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF');
REPLACE INTO `concept_description` (`concept_description_id`, `concept_id`, `description`, `locale`, `creator`, `date_created`, `changed_by`, `date_changed`, `uuid`) values('12606','140514','Inflammation of the fascia. There are three major types: 1) Eosinophilic fasciitis, an inflammatory reaction with eosinophilia, producing hard thickened skin with an orange-peel configuration suggestive of scleroderma and considered by some a variant of scleroderma; 2) Necrotizing fasciitis (FASCIITIS, NECROTIZING), a serious fulminating infection (usually by a beta hemolytic streptococcus) causing extensive necrosis of superficial fascia; 3) Nodular/Pseudosarcomatous /Proliferative fasciitis, characterized by a rapid growth of fibroblasts with mononuclear inflammatory cells and proliferating capillaries in soft tissue, often the forearm; it is not malignant but is sometimes mistaken for fibrosarcoma.','en','1','2007-10-18 04:28:24','1',NULL,'12606FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF');
REPLACE INTO `concept_description` (`concept_description_id`, `concept_id`, `description`, `locale`, `creator`, `date_created`, `changed_by`, `date_changed`, `uuid`) values('12607','140515','Involuntary contraction of the muscle fibers innervated by a motor unit. Fasciculations can often by visualized and take the form of a muscle twitch or dimpling under the skin, but usually do not generate sufficient force to move a limb. They may represent a benign condition or occur as a manifestation of MOTOR NEURON DISEASE or PERIPHERAL NERVOUS SYSTEM DISEASES. (Adams et al., Principles of Neurology, 6th ed, p1294)','en','1','2007-10-18 04:28:24','1',NULL,'12607FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF');
REPLACE INTO `concept_description` (`concept_description_id`, `concept_id`, `description`, `locale`, `creator`, `date_created`, `changed_by`, `date_changed`, `uuid`) values('12608','140517','Conditions in which inhalation of organic dusts results in hypersensitivity reactions at the alveolar level, associated with the production of precipitins.','en','1','2007-10-18 04:28:24','1',NULL,'12608FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF');
REPLACE INTO `concept_description` (`concept_description_id`, `concept_id`, `description`, `locale`, `creator`, `date_created`, `changed_by`, `date_changed`, `uuid`) values('12609','140519','Congenital hypoplastic anemia, probably hereditary, with multiple abnormalities.','en','1','2007-10-18 04:28:24','1',NULL,'12609FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF');
REPLACE INTO `concept_description` (`concept_description_id`, `concept_id`, `description`, `locale`, `creator`, `date_created`, `changed_by`, `date_changed`, `uuid`) values('12610','140520','Constellation of clinical and laboratory manifestations produced by generalized proximal tubular insufficiency in the presence of normal, or nearly normal, glomerular filtration.','en','1','2007-10-18 04:28:24','1',NULL,'12610FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF');
REPLACE INTO `concept_description` (`concept_description_id`, `concept_id`, `description`, `locale`, `creator`, `date_created`, `changed_by`, `date_changed`, `uuid`) values('12611','140521','A personality disorder characterized by the avoidance of accepting deserved blame and an unwarranted view of others as malevolent. The latter is expressed as suspiciousness, hypersensitivity, and mistrust.','en','1','2007-10-18 04:28:24','1',NULL,'12611FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF');
REPLACE INTO `concept_description` (`concept_description_id`, `concept_id`, `description`, `locale`, `creator`, `date_created`, `changed_by`, `date_changed`, `uuid`) values('12613','140538','Familial disorder characterized by hypophosphatemia associated with decreased renal tubular reabsorption of inorganic phosphorus. It is sometimes associated with osteomalacia or rickets which do not respond to the usual doses of vitamin D.','en','1','2007-10-18 04:28:24','1',NULL,'12613FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF');
REPLACE INTO `concept_description` (`concept_description_id`, `concept_id`, `description`, `locale`, `creator`, `date_created`, `changed_by`, `date_changed`, `uuid`) values('12614','140540','A group of conditions of diverse etiologies characterized by the accumulation of insoluble fibrillar proteins (amyloid) in various organs and tissues of the body such that vital function is compromised. The associated disease states may be inflammatory, hereditary, or neoplastic, and the deposition can be localized or generalized or systemic. (Dorland, 27th ed)','en','1','2007-10-18 04:28:24','1',NULL,'12614FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF');
REPLACE INTO `concept_description` (`concept_description_id`, `concept_id`, `description`, `locale`, `creator`, `date_created`, `changed_by`, `date_changed`, `uuid`) values('12615','140542','Glycosuria occurring when there is only the normal amount of sugar in the blood, due to inherited inability of the renal tubules to reabsorb glucose completely. (Dorland, 27th ed)','en','1','2007-10-18 04:28:24','1',NULL,'12615FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF');
REPLACE INTO `concept_description` (`concept_description_id`, `concept_id`, `description`, `locale`, `creator`, `date_created`, `changed_by`, `date_changed`, `uuid`) values('12616','140543','A group of disorders characterized by the excessive production of porphyrins or their precursors that arises from abnormalities in the regulation of the porphyrin-heme pathway. The porphyrias are usually divided into three broad groups, erythropoietic (PORPHYRIA, ERYTHROPOIETIC), hepatic (PORPHYRIA, HEPATIC), and erythrohepatic (PORPHYRIA, ERYTHROHEPATIC), according to the major sites of abnormal porphyrin synthesis.','en','1','2007-10-18 04:28:24','1',NULL,'12616FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF');
REPLACE INTO `concept_description` (`concept_description_id`, `concept_id`, `description`, `locale`, `creator`, `date_created`, `changed_by`, `date_changed`, `uuid`) values('12617','140544','A heterogenous group of inherited disorders characterized by recurring attacks of rapidly progressive flaccid paralysis or myotonia. These conditions have in common a mutation of the gene encoding the alpha subunit of the sodium channel in skeletal muscle. They are frequently associated with fluctuations in serum potassium levels. Periodic paralysis may also occur as a non-familial process secondary to THYROTOXICOSIS and other conditions. (From Adams et al., Principles of Neurology, 6th ed, p1481)','en','1','2007-10-18 04:28:24','1',NULL,'12617FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF');
REPLACE INTO `concept_description` (`concept_description_id`, `concept_id`, `description`, `locale`, `creator`, `date_created`, `changed_by`, `date_changed`, `uuid`) values('12618','140545','Presence of fluid within the pericardium.','en','1','2007-10-18 04:28:24','1',NULL,'12618FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF');
REPLACE INTO `concept_description` (`concept_description_id`, `concept_id`, `description`, `locale`, `creator`, `date_created`, `changed_by`, `date_changed`, `uuid`) values('12619','140546','A collection of rare conditions resulting from defective fat metabolism and characterized by atrophy of the subcutaneous fat. They include total, congenital or acquired, partial, abdominal infantile, and localized lipodystrophy.','en','1','2007-10-18 04:28:24','1',NULL,'12619FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF');
REPLACE INTO `concept_description` (`concept_description_id`, `concept_id`, `description`, `locale`, `creator`, `date_created`, `changed_by`, `date_changed`, `uuid`) values('12620','140548','Increase in body weight beyond skeletal and physical standards as the result of an excessive accumulation of fat in the body. More than two times the ideal weight is considered OBESITY, MORBID.','en','1','2007-10-18 04:28:24','1',NULL,'12620FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF');
REPLACE INTO `concept_description` (`concept_description_id`, `concept_id`, `description`, `locale`, `creator`, `date_created`, `changed_by`, `date_changed`, `uuid`) values('12621','140549','A heterogenous group of inherited disorders characterized by recurring attacks of rapidly progressive flaccid paralysis or myotonia. These conditions have in common a mutation of the gene encoding the alpha subunit of the sodium channel in skeletal muscle. They are frequently associated with fluctuations in serum potassium levels. Periodic paralysis may also occur as a non-familial process secondary to THYROTOXICOSIS and other conditions. (From Adams et al., Principles of Neurology, 6th ed, p1481)','en','1','2007-10-18 04:28:24','1',NULL,'12621FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF');
REPLACE INTO `concept_description` (`concept_description_id`, `concept_id`, `description`, `locale`, `creator`, `date_created`, `changed_by`, `date_changed`, `uuid`) values('12622','140550','A decrease in the number of GRANULOCYTES (BASOPHILS, EOSINOPHILS, and NEUTROPHILS).','en','1','2007-10-18 04:28:24','1',NULL,'12622FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF');
REPLACE INTO `concept_description` (`concept_description_id`, `concept_id`, `description`, `locale`, `creator`, `date_created`, `changed_by`, `date_changed`, `uuid`) values('12623','140553','A disorder genetically distinct from the other inherited hyperlipidemias characterized by the type II or type IV lipoprotein pattern (the pattern may change from time to time and the lipid level may be normal at one time and abnormal at another time).','en','1','2007-10-18 04:28:24','1',NULL,'12623FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF');
REPLACE INTO `concept_description` (`concept_description_id`, `concept_id`, `description`, `locale`, `creator`, `date_created`, `changed_by`, `date_changed`, `uuid`) values('12624','140561','A megaloblastic anemia occurring in children but more commonly in later life, characterized by histamine-fast achlorhydria, in which the laboratory and clinical manifestations are based on malabsorption of vitamin B 12 due to a failure of the gastric mucosa to secrete adequate and potent intrinsic factor. (Dorland, 27th ed)','en','1','2007-10-18 04:28:24','1',NULL,'12624FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF');
REPLACE INTO `concept_description` (`concept_description_id`, `concept_id`, `description`, `locale`, `creator`, `date_created`, `changed_by`, `date_changed`, `uuid`) values('12625','140562','An autosomal recessive inherited disease characterized by episodic fever, severe abdominal pain, pleurisy, arthritis, and a characteristic ankle rash. Disease flare-ups tend to last 3 days, and individuals are asymptomatic between attacks. Orchitis, a benign recurrent MENINGITIS, headaches, and amyloid nephropathy may also occur. (From Medicine (Baltimore) 1998 Jul;77(4):268-97)','en','1','2007-10-18 04:28:24','1',NULL,'12625FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF');
REPLACE INTO `concept_description` (`concept_description_id`, `concept_id`, `description`, `locale`, `creator`, `date_created`, `changed_by`, `date_changed`, `uuid`) values('12626','140563','A rare familial condition characterized by massive chylomicronemia and decreased levels of other lipoproteins. It is due to deficiency of lipoprotein lipase, an alkaline triglyceride hydrolase which catalyzes an important step in the extrahepatic removal of triglyceride-rich lipoproteins from the blood.','en','1','2007-10-18 04:28:24','1',NULL,'12626FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF');
REPLACE INTO `concept_description` (`concept_description_id`, `concept_id`, `description`, `locale`, `creator`, `date_created`, `changed_by`, `date_changed`, `uuid`) values('12627','140564','The presence of abnormally low levels of lipoproteins in the serum.','en','1','2007-10-18 04:28:24','1',NULL,'12627FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF');
REPLACE INTO `concept_description` (`concept_description_id`, `concept_id`, `description`, `locale`, `creator`, `date_created`, `changed_by`, `date_changed`, `uuid`) values('12628','140565','Hereditary metabolic disorder characterized by recurrent acute arthritis, hyperuricemia and deposition of sodium urate in and around the joints, sometimes with formation of uric acid calculi.','en','1','2007-10-18 04:28:24','1',NULL,'12628FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF');
REPLACE INTO `concept_description` (`concept_description_id`, `concept_id`, `description`, `locale`, `creator`, `date_created`, `changed_by`, `date_changed`, `uuid`) values('12629','140566','Diffuse or local inflammation and edema of the interstitial tissue of the kidney, including the tubules.','en','1','2007-10-18 04:28:24','1',NULL,'12629FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF');
REPLACE INTO `concept_description` (`concept_description_id`, `concept_id`, `description`, `locale`, `creator`, `date_created`, `changed_by`, `date_changed`, `uuid`) values('12630','140568','A pathological condition that removes acid or adds base to the body fluids.','en','1','2007-10-18 04:28:24','1',NULL,'12630FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF');
REPLACE INTO `concept_description` (`concept_description_id`, `concept_id`, `description`, `locale`, `creator`, `date_created`, `changed_by`, `date_changed`, `uuid`) values('12631','140571','Abnormally increased activity of the parathyroid glands, which may be primary or secondary (HYPERPARATHYRODISM, SECONDARY). Primary hyperparathyroidism is associated with neoplasia or hyperplasia. The excess of parathyroid hormone leads to alteration in function of bone, renal tubules, and gastrointestinal mucosa. (Dorland, 27th ed)','en','1','2007-10-18 04:28:24','1',NULL,'12631FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF');
REPLACE INTO `concept_description` (`concept_description_id`, `concept_id`, `description`, `locale`, `creator`, `date_created`, `changed_by`, `date_changed`, `uuid`) values('12632','140572','The presence of abnormally low levels of lipoproteins in the serum.','en','1','2007-10-18 04:28:24','1',NULL,'12632FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF');
REPLACE INTO `concept_description` (`concept_description_id`, `concept_id`, `description`, `locale`, `creator`, `date_created`, `changed_by`, `date_changed`, `uuid`) values('12633','140573','A familial disorder characterized by an isolated elevation in the plasma level of endogenously synthesized triglyceride carried in VLDL. It is considered to be an autosomal dominant trait.','en','1','2007-10-18 04:28:24','1',NULL,'12633FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF');
REPLACE INTO `concept_description` (`concept_description_id`, `concept_id`, `description`, `locale`, `creator`, `date_created`, `changed_by`, `date_changed`, `uuid`) values('12634','140574','Abnormally increased activity of the parathyroid glands, which may be primary or secondary (HYPERPARATHYRODISM, SECONDARY). Primary hyperparathyroidism is associated with neoplasia or hyperplasia. The excess of parathyroid hormone leads to alteration in function of bone, renal tubules, and gastrointestinal mucosa. (Dorland, 27th ed)','en','1','2007-10-18 04:28:24','1',NULL,'12634FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF');
REPLACE INTO `concept_description` (`concept_description_id`, `concept_id`, `description`, `locale`, `creator`, `date_created`, `changed_by`, `date_changed`, `uuid`) values('12635','140575','A rare familial condition characterized by massive chylomicronemia and decreased levels of other lipoproteins. It is due to deficiency of lipoprotein lipase, an alkaline triglyceride hydrolase which catalyzes an important step in the extrahepatic removal of triglyceride-rich lipoproteins from the blood.','en','1','2007-10-18 04:28:24','1',NULL,'12635FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF');
REPLACE INTO `concept_description` (`concept_description_id`, `concept_id`, `description`, `locale`, `creator`, `date_created`, `changed_by`, `date_changed`, `uuid`) values('12636','140576','A heterogenous group of inherited disorders characterized by recurring attacks of rapidly progressive flaccid paralysis or myotonia. These conditions have in common a mutation of the gene encoding the alpha subunit of the sodium channel in skeletal muscle. They are frequently associated with fluctuations in serum potassium levels. Periodic paralysis may also occur as a non-familial process secondary to THYROTOXICOSIS and other conditions. (From Adams et al., Principles of Neurology, 6th ed, p1481)','en','1','2007-10-18 04:28:24','1',NULL,'12636FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF');
REPLACE INTO `concept_description` (`concept_description_id`, `concept_id`, `description`, `locale`, `creator`, `date_created`, `changed_by`, `date_changed`, `uuid`) values('12637','140579','Group of disorders which feature accumulations of active histiocytes and lymphocytes, but where the histiocytes are not Langerhans cells.  The group includes hemophagocytic lymphohistiocytosis, infection-associated hemophagocytic syndrome, sinus histiocytosis, xanthogranuloma, reticulohistiocytoma, juvenile xanthoma, xanthoma disseminatum, as well as the lipid storage diseases (sea-blue histiocyte syndrome and Niemann-Pick disease).','en','1','2007-10-18 04:28:24','1',NULL,'12637FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF');
REPLACE INTO `concept_description` (`concept_description_id`, `concept_id`, `description`, `locale`, `creator`, `date_created`, `changed_by`, `date_changed`, `uuid`) values('12638','140580','A condition characterized by throbbing headaches which are preceded or accompanied by reversible symptoms that reflect cortical or brain stem dysfunction. The most common type of aura consists of a positive visual phenomenon, usually in the form of a scintillating scotoma. An aura may also take the form of other focal neurologic symptoms or signs, including loss of sensation or weakness in an extremity. In general, the aura precedes the headache by less than 60 minutes, develops over 4 minutes or longer, and has a duration of less than one hour. (From Adams et al., Principles of Neurology, 6th ed, p172; Cephalalgia 1988;8:Suppl 7:1-96)','en','1','2007-10-18 04:28:24','1',NULL,'12638FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF');
REPLACE INTO `concept_description` (`concept_description_id`, `concept_id`, `description`, `locale`, `creator`, `date_created`, `changed_by`, `date_changed`, `uuid`) values('12639','140582','A collection of rare conditions resulting from defective fat metabolism and characterized by atrophy of the subcutaneous fat. They include total, congenital or acquired, partial, abdominal infantile, and localized lipodystrophy.','en','1','2007-10-18 04:28:24','1',NULL,'12639FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF');
REPLACE INTO `concept_description` (`concept_description_id`, `concept_id`, `description`, `locale`, `creator`, `date_created`, `changed_by`, `date_changed`, `uuid`) values('12640','140583','Involuntary shock-like contractions, irregular in rhythm and amplitude, followed by relaxation, of a muscle or a group of muscles. This condition may be a feature of some CENTRAL NERVOUS SYSTEMS DISEASES (e.g., EPILEPSY, MYOCLONIC). Nocturnal myoclonus may represent a normal physiologic event or occur as the principal feature of the NOCTURNAL MYOCLONUS SYNDROME. (From Adams et al., Principles of Neurology, 6th ed, pp102-3).','en','1','2007-10-18 04:28:24','1',NULL,'12640FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF');
REPLACE INTO `concept_description` (`concept_description_id`, `concept_id`, `description`, `locale`, `creator`, `date_created`, `changed_by`, `date_changed`, `uuid`) values('12641','140584','Abnormal increase in eosinophils in the blood, tissues or organs.','en','1','2007-10-18 04:28:24','1',NULL,'12641FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF');
REPLACE INTO `concept_description` (`concept_description_id`, `concept_id`, `description`, `locale`, `creator`, `date_created`, `changed_by`, `date_changed`, `uuid`) values('12642','140585','An autosomal disorder of the peripheral and autonomic nervous systems limited to individuals of Ashkenazic Jewish descent. Clinical manifestations are present at birth and include diminished lacrimation, defective thermoregulation, orthostatic hypotension (HYPOTENSION, ORTHOSTATIC), fixed pupils, excessive SWEATING, loss of pain and temperature sensation, and absent reflexes. Pathologic features include reduced numbers of small diameter peripheral nerve fibers and autonomic ganglion neurons. (From Adams et al., Principles of Neurology, 6th ed, p1348; Nat Genet 1993;4(2):160-4)','en','1','2007-10-18 04:28:24','1',NULL,'12642FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF');
REPLACE INTO `concept_description` (`concept_description_id`, `concept_id`, `description`, `locale`, `creator`, `date_created`, `changed_by`, `date_changed`, `uuid`) values('12643','140589','A metabolic disorder due to disorders in the production or release of vasopressin. It is characterized by the chronic excretion of large amounts of low specific gravity urine and great thirst.','en','1','2007-10-18 04:28:24','1',NULL,'12643FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF');
REPLACE INTO `concept_description` (`concept_description_id`, `concept_id`, `description`, `locale`, `creator`, `date_created`, `changed_by`, `date_changed`, `uuid`) values('12644','140593','Rare hereditary disease characterized by recurrent eruptions of vesicles and bullae mainly on the neck, axillae, and groin. It exhibits autosomal dominant inheritance and is unrelated to pemphigus vulgaris though it closely resembles that disease.','en','1','2007-10-18 04:28:24','1',NULL,'12644FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF');
REPLACE INTO `concept_description` (`concept_description_id`, `concept_id`, `description`, `locale`, `creator`, `date_created`, `changed_by`, `date_changed`, `uuid`) values('12645','140594','Abnormally increased activity of the parathyroid glands, which may be primary or secondary (HYPERPARATHYRODISM, SECONDARY). Primary hyperparathyroidism is associated with neoplasia or hyperplasia. The excess of parathyroid hormone leads to alteration in function of bone, renal tubules, and gastrointestinal mucosa. (Dorland, 27th ed)','en','1','2007-10-18 04:28:24','1',NULL,'12645FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF');
REPLACE INTO `concept_description` (`concept_description_id`, `concept_id`, `description`, `locale`, `creator`, `date_created`, `changed_by`, `date_changed`, `uuid`) values('12646','140596','A rare familial condition characterized by massive chylomicronemia and decreased levels of other lipoproteins. It is due to deficiency of lipoprotein lipase, an alkaline triglyceride hydrolase which catalyzes an important step in the extrahepatic removal of triglyceride-rich lipoproteins from the blood.','en','1','2007-10-18 04:28:24','1',NULL,'12646FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF');
REPLACE INTO `concept_description` (`concept_description_id`, `concept_id`, `description`, `locale`, `creator`, `date_created`, `changed_by`, `date_changed`, `uuid`) values('12647','140598','A skin and mucous membrane disease characterized by an eruption of macules, papules, nodules, vesicles, and/or bullae with characteristic \"bull\'s-eye\" lesions usually occurring on the dorsal aspect of the hands and forearms.','en','1','2007-10-18 04:28:24','1',NULL,'12647FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF');
REPLACE INTO `concept_description` (`concept_description_id`, `concept_id`, `description`, `locale`, `creator`, `date_created`, `changed_by`, `date_changed`, `uuid`) values('12648','140599','A group of conditions of diverse etiologies characterized by the accumulation of insoluble fibrillar proteins (amyloid) in various organs and tissues of the body such that vital function is compromised. The associated disease states may be inflammatory, hereditary, or neoplastic, and the deposition can be localized or generalized or systemic. (Dorland, 27th ed)','en','1','2007-10-18 04:28:24','1',NULL,'12648FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF');
REPLACE INTO `concept_description` (`concept_description_id`, `concept_id`, `description`, `locale`, `creator`, `date_created`, `changed_by`, `date_changed`, `uuid`) values('12649','140600','Disorders of the peripheral nervous system associated with the deposition of AMYLOID in nerve tissue. Familial, primary (nonfamilial), and secondary forms have been described. Some familial subtypes demonstrate an autosomal dominant pattern of inheritance. Clinical manifestations include sensory loss, mild weakness, autonomic dysfunction, and CARPAL TUNNEL SYNDROME. (Adams et al., Principles of Neurology, 6th ed, p1349)','en','1','2007-10-18 04:28:24','1',NULL,'12649FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF');
REPLACE INTO `concept_description` (`concept_description_id`, `concept_id`, `description`, `locale`, `creator`, `date_created`, `changed_by`, `date_changed`, `uuid`) values('12650','140601','Disorders of the peripheral nervous system associated with the deposition of AMYLOID in nerve tissue. Familial, primary (nonfamilial), and secondary forms have been described. Some familial subtypes demonstrate an autosomal dominant pattern of inheritance. Clinical manifestations include sensory loss, mild weakness, autonomic dysfunction, and CARPAL TUNNEL SYNDROME. (Adams et al., Principles of Neurology, 6th ed, p1349)','en','1','2007-10-18 04:28:24','1',NULL,'12650FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF');
