REPLACE INTO `concept_description` (`concept_description_id`, `concept_id`, `description`, `locale`, `creator`, `date_created`, `changed_by`, `date_changed`, `uuid`) values('14639','147243','A fungal infection that may appear in two forms: 1) a primary lesion characterized by the formation of a small cutaneous nodule and small nodules along the lymphatics that may heal within several months; and 2) chronic granulomatous lesions characterized by thick crusts, warty growths, and unusual vascularity and infection in the middle or upper lobes of the lung.','en','1','2007-10-18 04:28:24','1','2015-04-06 14:07:00','14639FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF');
REPLACE INTO `concept_description` (`concept_description_id`, `concept_id`, `description`, `locale`, `creator`, `date_created`, `changed_by`, `date_changed`, `uuid`) values('14640','147244','Injuries resulting when a person is struck by particles impelled with violent force from an explosion. Blast causes pulmonary concussion and hemorrhage, laceration of other thoracic and abdominal viscera, ruptured ear drums, and minor effects in the central nevous system. (From Dorland, 27th ed)','en','1','2007-10-18 04:28:24','1',NULL,'14640FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF');
REPLACE INTO `concept_description` (`concept_description_id`, `concept_id`, `description`, `locale`, `creator`, `date_created`, `changed_by`, `date_changed`, `uuid`) values('14641','147251','An abnormal passage in the bladder or between the bladder and any surrounding organ.','en','1','2007-10-18 04:28:24','1',NULL,'14641FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF');
REPLACE INTO `concept_description` (`concept_description_id`, `concept_id`, `description`, `locale`, `creator`, `date_created`, `changed_by`, `date_changed`, `uuid`) values('14643','147259','A transient loss of consciousness and postural tone caused by diminished blood flow to the brain (i.e., BRAIN ISCHEMIA). Presyncope refers to the sensation of lightheadedness and loss of strength that precedes a syncopal event or accompanies an incomplete syncope. (From Adams et al., Principles of Neurology, 6th ed, pp367-9)','en','1','2007-10-18 04:28:24','1',NULL,'14643FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF');
REPLACE INTO `concept_description` (`concept_description_id`, `concept_id`, `description`, `locale`, `creator`, `date_created`, `changed_by`, `date_changed`, `uuid`) values('14644','147260','A complication of MALARIA, FALCIPARUM characterized by the passage of dark red to black urine.','en','1','2007-10-18 04:28:24','1',NULL,'14644FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF');
REPLACE INTO `concept_description` (`concept_description_id`, `concept_id`, `description`, `locale`, `creator`, `date_created`, `changed_by`, `date_changed`, `uuid`) values('14645','147261','Either of two diseases resulting from fungal infection of the hair shafts. Black piedra occurs mainly in and on the hairs of the scalp and is caused by Piedraia hortae; white piedra occurs in and on the hairs of the scalp, beard, moustache and genital areas and is caused by Trichosporon beigelii.','en','1','2007-10-18 04:28:24','1',NULL,'14645FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF');
REPLACE INTO `concept_description` (`concept_description_id`, `concept_id`, `description`, `locale`, `creator`, `date_created`, `changed_by`, `date_changed`, `uuid`) values('14646','147263','A benign condition of the tongue characterized by hypertrophy of the filiform papillae that give the dorsum of the tongue a furry appearance. The color of the elongated papillae varies from yellowish white to brown or black, depending upon staining by substances such as tobacco, food, or drugs. (Dorland, 27th ed)','en','1','2007-10-18 04:28:24','1',NULL,'14646FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF');
REPLACE INTO `concept_description` (`concept_description_id`, `concept_id`, `description`, `locale`, `creator`, `date_created`, `changed_by`, `date_changed`, `uuid`) values('14647','147264','A localized defect in the visual field bordered by an area of normal vision. This occurs with a variety of EYE DISEASES (e.g., RETINAL DISEASES and GLAUCOMA), OPTIC NERVE DISEASES, and other conditions.','en','1','2007-10-18 04:28:24','1',NULL,'14647FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF');
REPLACE INTO `concept_description` (`concept_description_id`, `concept_id`, `description`, `locale`, `creator`, `date_created`, `changed_by`, `date_changed`, `uuid`) values('14648','147267','A nutritional condition produced by a deficiency of VITAMIN A in the diet, characterized by NIGHT BLINDNESS and other ocular manifestations such as dryness of the conjunctiva and later of the cornea (XEROPHTHALMIA). Vitamin A deficiency is a very common problem worldwide, particularly in developing countries as a consequence of famine or shortages of vitamin A-rich foods. In the United States it is found among the urban poor, the elderly, alcoholics, and patients with malabsorption. (From Cecil Textbook of Medicine, 19th ed, p1179)','en','1','2007-10-18 04:28:24','1','2012-11-02 23:56:04','14648FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF');
REPLACE INTO `concept_description` (`concept_description_id`, `concept_id`, `description`, `locale`, `creator`, `date_created`, `changed_by`, `date_changed`, `uuid`) values('14649','147268','Partial or complete loss of vision in one half of the visual field(s) of one or both eyes. Subtypes include altitudinal hemianopsia, characterized by a visual defect above or below the horizontal meridian of the visual field. Homonymous hemianopsia refers to a visual defect that affects both eyes equally, and occurs either to the left or right of the midline of the visual field. Binasal hemianopsia consists of loss of vision in the nasal hemifields of both eyes. Bitemporal hemianopsia is the bilateral loss of vision in the temporal fields. Quadrantanopsia refers to loss of vision in one quarter of the visual field in one or both eyes.','en','1','2007-10-18 04:28:24','1',NULL,'14649FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF');
REPLACE INTO `concept_description` (`concept_description_id`, `concept_id`, `description`, `locale`, `creator`, `date_created`, `changed_by`, `date_changed`, `uuid`) values('14650','147277','Mechanical or anoxic trauma incurred by the infant during labor or delivery.','en','1','2007-10-18 04:28:24','1',NULL,'14650FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF');
